WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:21.314
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:21.584 --> 00:24.254
TOKYO

3
00:47.152 --> 00:48.570
Mom, Dad…

4
00:53.241 --> 00:55.702
Mom… Mom!

5
00:55.785 --> 00:59.122
Please don't. Please!

6
02:21.079 --> 02:22.830
THE BLUE ROAD

7
02:25.333 --> 02:29.295
BOYS' HIGH JUMP, JUNIOR HIGH DIVISION FIRST PLACE, INOSE HIROSHI

8
02:53.027 --> 02:53.945
Hello?

9
02:54.445 --> 02:57.365
Sir, there's been a murder in Shinjuku.

10
02:58.199 --> 03:01.077
We're securing the crime scene, so please come quickly.

11
03:01.160 --> 03:02.412
Yeah, got it.

12
03:20.430 --> 03:22.515
No photos, please.

13
03:22.598 --> 03:25.351
What's going on?

14
03:25.435 --> 03:27.770
Please don't take pictures. Sorry.

15
03:41.284 --> 03:43.119
I want to clock out already.

16
03:49.751 --> 03:51.044
I'm sorry, sir.

17
03:51.961 --> 03:53.296
What's your business here?

18
03:53.796 --> 03:55.548
I'm with the Investigations Division.

19
03:55.631 --> 03:57.467
In that case, could I see your badge?

20
03:57.550 --> 03:58.718
My badge?

21
03:59.218 --> 04:01.012
I forgot it. Am I good to come in?

22
04:02.055 --> 04:02.889
Sorry?

23
04:03.473 --> 04:04.599
Can I come in?

24
04:05.183 --> 04:06.809
-Yes. -What do you mean "yes"?

25
04:07.643 --> 04:09.937
You should check my ID before letting me in.

26
04:10.813 --> 04:11.647
Sir.

27
04:12.774 --> 04:14.484
Is this how you secure a crime scene?

28
04:14.567 --> 04:15.735
My bad, sir.

29
04:19.030 --> 04:21.032
Is this how you secure a crime scene?

30
04:21.115 --> 04:23.117
My apologies!

31
04:31.709 --> 04:34.003
You know that huge fire two years ago?

32
04:34.087 --> 04:36.005
The one with all the fatalities.

33
04:36.089 --> 04:39.175
This is the building, left abandoned after the fire.

34
04:39.675 --> 04:43.096
Officers from the nearby station responded to a call and found the body.

35
04:43.179 --> 04:46.015
Since then, we've been unable to reach the caller.

36
04:47.141 --> 04:50.937
ONE FEAR BREEDS INFINITE FEAR AND ALL METHODS SHALL BE CONCEALED

37
04:53.648 --> 04:54.899
It's Hangeul.

38
04:54.982 --> 04:56.526
What does it say?

39
04:57.443 --> 04:59.612
An expert is on their way to confirm.

40
05:00.113 --> 05:02.740
Why didn't you call one sooner?

41
05:02.824 --> 05:04.033
My apologies, sir.

42
05:27.473 --> 05:28.683
The victim's identity?

43
05:29.183 --> 05:31.727
A female, believed to be in her teens or twenties.

44
05:31.811 --> 05:35.356
The estimated time of death is at least 24 hours ago.

45
05:35.440 --> 05:37.233
They found no signs of sexual assault

46
05:37.316 --> 05:39.444
but did find traces of drugs in her system.

47
05:39.527 --> 05:41.404
At least 100 milligrams.

48
05:42.196 --> 05:46.451
So her limbs were broken while she was still alive, not after she was killed?

49
05:46.534 --> 05:47.368
Yes.

50
05:47.452 --> 05:52.415
Is a human really capable of this? That's an insane amount of strength.

51
05:52.915 --> 05:54.041
It appears as though

52
05:55.042 --> 05:56.627
they used some kind of tool.

53
05:58.087 --> 05:59.630
A tool?

54
06:14.937 --> 06:15.771
Sir.

55
06:16.272 --> 06:18.107
-Yeah? -What's wrong?

56
06:19.692 --> 06:21.152
It's nothing. Let's go.

57
06:30.995 --> 06:33.539
Surely, no perpetrator would throw up at the scene…

58
06:36.542 --> 06:37.919
Bean sprouts?

59
06:38.669 --> 06:40.338
Kimchi? Or maybe yakiniku?

60
06:41.339 --> 06:43.090
And we can't reach the caller?

61
06:43.174 --> 06:46.677
No, sir. We'll check with nearby stores and homeless people in the area.

62
06:46.761 --> 06:49.597
What homeless person eats yakiniku? Send this to forensics.

63
06:50.890 --> 06:51.849
Yes, sir.

64
06:53.518 --> 06:56.479
There should be some junkies who use this place as a hangout.

65
06:57.021 --> 07:00.107
They must have called it in and then made a run for it.

66
07:00.191 --> 07:03.194
Of course, sir! I'll look into local junkies too.

67
07:03.903 --> 07:05.071
Excuse me.

68
07:06.531 --> 07:08.074
What were you doing?

69
07:08.157 --> 07:10.076
That's a camera, is it not?

70
07:10.576 --> 07:12.828
Would you mind if I took a quick look?

71
07:13.329 --> 07:15.248
These darn reporters.

72
07:15.831 --> 07:18.334
Can you please hurry it up?

73
07:24.966 --> 07:27.218
Hey. What are you doing?

74
07:27.301 --> 07:29.554
Please don't mess around.

75
07:33.474 --> 07:37.103
That's enough, sir. Mind if I quickly check your bag myself?

76
07:37.186 --> 07:38.312
Yes, sir.

77
07:39.939 --> 07:40.773
Hey!

78
07:42.858 --> 07:43.693
Let go!

79
07:45.236 --> 07:46.988
What are you playing at?

80
08:00.042 --> 08:02.670
Hey!

81
08:03.170 --> 08:04.422
Wait!

82
08:05.756 --> 08:06.757
Wait!

83
08:07.341 --> 08:08.426
Idiots.

84
08:09.468 --> 08:10.469
Stop!

85
08:16.017 --> 08:17.310
Why are you running away?

86
08:20.438 --> 08:22.315
-Sorry. -Watch where you're going!

87
08:24.358 --> 08:25.526
What the hell?

88
08:27.903 --> 08:29.071
Hey!

89
08:30.573 --> 08:31.407
Hey!

90
08:41.292 --> 08:43.753
Someone call the cops!

91
08:54.138 --> 08:54.972
I've got you now!

92
09:18.329 --> 09:19.497
This ends here.

93
09:41.185 --> 09:42.311
Hey, careful.

94
09:42.395 --> 09:43.229
You're Korean?

95
09:51.237 --> 09:52.530
Hold on.

96
09:53.114 --> 09:53.948
What?

97
09:59.745 --> 10:01.914
Don't move! Hands up!

98
10:04.959 --> 10:06.502
Sir, are you okay?

99
10:09.797 --> 10:14.176
TOKYO METROPOLITAN POLICE DEPARTMENT

100
10:14.260 --> 10:17.221
INVESTIGATIONS DIVISION 1

101
10:24.353 --> 10:26.147
-Good morning. -Good morning.

102
10:27.523 --> 10:28.691
Good morning.

103
10:29.734 --> 10:32.945
Apparently, Inose's team pulled another all-nighter.

104
10:33.946 --> 10:35.448
They've been here all night?

105
10:45.207 --> 10:47.460
So you took pictures of the scene with this.

106
10:57.845 --> 10:59.555
Why did you take these pictures?

107
11:01.140 --> 11:02.892
You're just going to stay silent?

108
11:03.392 --> 11:06.187
Answer me!

109
11:06.687 --> 11:08.773
Sagawa, lift.

110
11:09.732 --> 11:11.066
Sir?

111
11:20.743 --> 11:22.453
I'll let it slide this time,

112
11:23.037 --> 11:25.039
but don't go waving a gun around like that.

113
11:26.207 --> 11:27.583
Got it, sir. Sorry.

114
11:28.083 --> 11:29.210
Hey, Korean.

115
11:30.211 --> 11:31.670
The sun's up, thanks to you.

116
11:32.171 --> 11:33.964
Don't you feel sorry at all?

117
11:36.467 --> 11:38.344
You must be the top dog here.

118
11:43.432 --> 11:44.934
And you're clearly a rookie.

119
11:46.894 --> 11:48.270
What did you just say?

120
11:48.354 --> 11:49.188
Hey, Korean!

121
11:49.772 --> 11:51.148
You killed her, didn't you?

122
11:51.649 --> 11:53.859
Answer me, dammit!

123
12:00.324 --> 12:01.450
You…

124
12:03.452 --> 12:05.120
know something, don't you?

125
12:07.164 --> 12:08.332
What now?

126
12:15.256 --> 12:16.590
My sincerest apologies

127
12:16.674 --> 12:21.804
for my subordinate's grave discourtesy.

128
12:21.887 --> 12:24.932
Please accept my apologies, Inspector Kim.

129
12:25.808 --> 12:28.936
What are you doing? Uncuff him now!

130
12:29.019 --> 12:29.854
Yes, sir.

131
12:31.522 --> 12:32.481
Here.

132
12:34.984 --> 12:36.569
He's an investigator from Korea.

133
12:36.652 --> 12:38.070
INTL. COOPERATION REQUEST

134
12:38.153 --> 12:39.363
An investigator?

135
12:39.446 --> 12:43.742
Korea just sent over an official cooperation request.

136
12:44.243 --> 12:47.121
Sagawa, go set up the conference room.

137
12:47.204 --> 12:48.080
Yes, sir.

138
13:01.010 --> 13:02.595
Allow me to introduce myself.

139
13:03.888 --> 13:07.308
I'm Detective Kim Seok from Seoul Police's Mobile Investigation Unit.

140
13:10.978 --> 13:13.272
If that's the case…

141
13:17.192 --> 13:19.236
you should have said so earlier.

142
13:20.237 --> 13:21.989
Why did you run away?

143
13:23.198 --> 13:27.536
I just wanted to see how Japanese cops treat Koreans. That a problem?

144
13:30.831 --> 13:31.707
Well, whatever.

145
13:31.790 --> 13:33.918
I was looking for the suspect's escape route.

146
13:35.169 --> 13:36.295
Looking for the escape--

147
13:36.378 --> 13:40.215
Yes. I was simply looking for the escape route, not running away.

148
13:43.928 --> 13:45.971
What an insufferable jerk.

149
13:46.055 --> 13:47.348
What's so insufferable?

150
13:49.141 --> 13:51.352
Is it wrong for a cop to be at a crime scene?

151
13:59.234 --> 14:02.905
So you can speak Japanese?

152
14:05.824 --> 14:07.826
-A little. -A little?

153
14:09.578 --> 14:11.121
Quit messing with me!

154
14:11.205 --> 14:12.790
Inose!

155
14:13.290 --> 14:14.416
That's enough!

156
14:23.759 --> 14:27.012
A similar murder took place in Korea recently.

157
14:27.513 --> 14:30.724
The victim's name was Park In-gyu. He went by the alias Cindy.

158
14:30.808 --> 14:32.017
He was 38 years old.

159
14:33.143 --> 14:36.105
He was a cross-dresser who worked in the nightlife industry.

160
14:37.189 --> 14:40.067
As you can see, the body was left

161
14:40.818 --> 14:43.404
as if it were a work of art on display for an audience.

162
14:43.904 --> 14:47.658
The victim's joints were all contorted in the opposite direction,

163
14:47.741 --> 14:51.495
and psychotropic drugs were found in his blood.

164
14:51.996 --> 14:55.207
It's a type of methamphetamine called Speed K,

165
14:55.290 --> 14:59.336
a new drug that's currently popular here in Tokyo, Japan.

166
14:59.420 --> 15:02.881
Speed K has also been spreading across Korea,

167
15:02.965 --> 15:05.926
so the Korean government is keeping a close eye on the situation.

168
15:06.010 --> 15:10.055
As for Park In-gyu, he is known to have visited Shinjuku to obtain the drug.

169
15:10.139 --> 15:12.307
That's why I was at the scene.

170
15:12.391 --> 15:15.102
While I was investigating,

171
15:15.894 --> 15:17.980
I happened to come across a body

172
15:18.063 --> 15:21.066
with limbs twisted in a manner very similar to Park In-gyu's.

173
15:22.359 --> 15:23.193
Typically…

174
15:23.277 --> 15:24.820
A coincidence?

175
15:24.903 --> 15:27.865
…murders of passion leave heavy, irregular blood spatters.

176
15:27.948 --> 15:30.451
You secured the crime scene, did you?

177
15:31.035 --> 15:32.077
I'm sorry, sir.

178
15:33.162 --> 15:36.248
Almost like an art gallery.

179
15:37.791 --> 15:38.876
And lastly,

180
15:40.294 --> 15:43.297
if you look at this message found at Park In-gyu's murder scene…

181
15:45.340 --> 15:48.635
This was also written in blood, just like at the Shinjuku crime scene.

182
15:50.429 --> 15:55.142
"One fear breeds infinite fear, and all methods shall be concealed."

183
15:55.893 --> 15:57.352
They both mean the same thing.

184
15:59.188 --> 16:00.898
So they mean the same thing?

185
16:04.943 --> 16:07.029
That's enough explaining. What's your point?

186
16:07.529 --> 16:09.948
That this is a serial murder spanning Japan and Korea?

187
16:10.949 --> 16:12.826
And the suspect's Korean, so you're here?

188
16:16.121 --> 16:20.125
In the Korean language, there is spacing between words.

189
16:20.834 --> 16:21.752
As you see here,

190
16:21.835 --> 16:24.671
the phrase was written without spaces, as is done in Japanese.

191
16:27.007 --> 16:29.218
So, in conclusion, we in Korea

192
16:30.302 --> 16:31.428
have identified

193
16:32.638 --> 16:33.889
the suspect as

194
16:34.973 --> 16:35.974
a Japanese national.

195
16:40.938 --> 16:42.439
Sagawa, Mikitani.

196
16:42.523 --> 16:45.025
-Bring me the forensics report. -Yes, sir.

197
16:45.109 --> 16:46.693
Okamoto, Hosaka.

198
16:46.777 --> 16:50.030
Search for any witnesses who were around at the time of the crime.

199
16:50.114 --> 16:50.948
Yes, sir.

200
16:54.701 --> 16:57.246
I'm telling you, we need to check the junkies.

201
17:00.290 --> 17:02.709
As for you…

202
17:06.505 --> 17:08.048
You're in charge of that Korean.

203
17:14.221 --> 17:16.181
Man, this sucks.

204
17:22.729 --> 17:24.064
Hey, Korean.

205
17:27.651 --> 17:30.070
You understand everything I'm saying, don't you?

206
17:32.990 --> 17:34.908
You're a loner, aren't you?

207
17:35.826 --> 17:37.327
That's why you're stuck with me.

208
17:40.747 --> 17:43.458
Detectives are lone wolves by nature.

209
17:44.418 --> 17:46.962
Anyway, you speak Japanese, right?

210
17:47.045 --> 17:49.298
Let's talk in Japanese from now on.

211
17:50.007 --> 17:51.884
Why should I do that?

212
17:54.052 --> 17:56.388
Because we Koreans all speak Japanese for you?

213
18:01.310 --> 18:02.811
I know Korean too.

214
18:04.563 --> 18:05.480
A little.

215
18:06.481 --> 18:07.858
Winter Sonata.

216
18:08.692 --> 18:09.943
Yonsama.

217
18:10.444 --> 18:11.278
See?

218
18:11.361 --> 18:13.572
Then I guess I can keep this brief.

219
18:14.781 --> 18:17.117
I'm not a big fan of working with a partner either.

220
18:26.293 --> 18:28.045
What's with that jerk?

221
18:33.050 --> 18:34.301
What a pain.

222
19:06.208 --> 19:07.960
NEW MESSAGE

223
19:08.043 --> 19:11.672
YOUR MOTHER'S BEEN QUITE DELIRIOUS LATELY IT MIGHT HELP IF YOU STOPPED BY

224
19:58.969 --> 20:00.012
Seok.

225
20:03.140 --> 20:04.391
Kim Seok.

226
20:08.937 --> 20:10.105
Kim Seok!

227
20:12.441 --> 20:13.483
Do not fear…

228
20:26.997 --> 20:30.250
SHINJUKU KABUKICHO

229
20:35.380 --> 20:38.133
Hey, kids. Have you seen this girl?

230
20:38.759 --> 20:39.885
She's super cute!

231
20:39.968 --> 20:42.220
Isn't that my mom? That's my mom.

232
20:42.304 --> 20:44.348
-How old are you? -I'm 20.

233
20:44.431 --> 20:46.183
Cut the crap.

234
20:48.435 --> 20:49.603
Hey, guys.

235
20:49.686 --> 20:50.896
Have you seen this girl?

236
20:50.979 --> 20:52.564
What?

237
20:53.231 --> 20:54.149
I think I know her.

238
20:54.232 --> 20:55.734
Really?

239
20:56.693 --> 20:59.237
Just kidding!

240
20:59.780 --> 21:02.991
What's that, you prick? "Just kidding"? You wanna try me?

241
21:16.254 --> 21:18.298
NO ENTRY

242
21:27.307 --> 21:30.060
Knock it off!

243
21:30.143 --> 21:32.187
You all look like you're having fun.

244
21:33.313 --> 21:34.147
Who are you?

245
21:34.231 --> 21:37.776
A random old guy. Recognize this girl? She was murdered recently.

246
21:37.859 --> 21:38.985
That's so scary!

247
21:39.069 --> 21:40.862
Was she really murdered?

248
21:45.117 --> 21:46.535
Wait.

249
21:47.035 --> 21:47.953
Isn't this Aki?

250
21:48.578 --> 21:49.454
Aki?

251
21:49.996 --> 21:51.581
No way. This is Aki?

252
21:51.665 --> 21:54.000
Yeah, look. There's a mole under her eye here.

253
21:54.084 --> 21:56.086
There's no way.

254
21:56.169 --> 21:58.296
Tell me more about this… Aki, you say?

255
21:58.964 --> 22:00.298
-That's her name? -I think so.

256
22:00.382 --> 22:04.136
Her name is Miyashita Aki. We hung out a few times.

257
22:04.219 --> 22:05.679
Whenever she got drunk,

258
22:05.762 --> 22:10.308
she'd start crying and say, "I wanna go home," or "I miss my parents."

259
22:10.392 --> 22:12.978
Isn't that hilarious?

260
22:13.061 --> 22:14.521
What is she, a kid?

261
22:14.604 --> 22:16.148
When did you last see her?

262
22:16.648 --> 22:19.985
The last time I saw her…

263
22:20.068 --> 22:21.570
Last Saturday, I think.

264
22:21.653 --> 22:23.697
I ran into her outside a karaoke bar,

265
22:23.780 --> 22:25.949
but she was with Takahashi, so we didn't talk.

266
22:26.032 --> 22:27.159
Takahashi?

267
22:27.242 --> 22:28.910
You're not meant to talk about him.

268
22:30.328 --> 22:31.955
You shouldn't have said that.

269
22:33.373 --> 22:35.125
-But you already did. -So out you go!

270
22:35.208 --> 22:36.751
Out you go!

271
22:36.835 --> 22:38.628
Bye-bye, mister!

272
22:38.712 --> 22:40.797
-Bye-bye, mister! -Okay!

273
22:40.881 --> 22:41.798
Thanks.

274
22:42.799 --> 22:43.758
Thank you.

275
22:45.677 --> 22:47.095
What the hell?

276
22:47.721 --> 22:49.097
Let go of me!

277
22:49.973 --> 22:51.892
What do you think you're doing, old man?

278
22:52.976 --> 22:55.353
-The hell do you think you are? -This is Speed K.

279
22:55.896 --> 22:57.522
Did you buy this from Takahashi?

280
22:58.106 --> 23:00.692
Please, let go of me!

281
23:01.193 --> 23:02.652
Where's Takahashi?

282
23:09.618 --> 23:12.746
Where can I find some more junkies to rip off, I wonder?

283
23:14.748 --> 23:16.208
Takahashi Shoma.

284
23:18.376 --> 23:19.544
Who the hell are you?

285
23:25.967 --> 23:26.968
So it is you.

286
23:28.595 --> 23:30.263
A Chōsenjin, are you?

287
23:30.847 --> 23:32.098
The hell do you want?

288
23:33.350 --> 23:34.684
This is self-defense.

289
23:37.103 --> 23:38.271
You son of a…

290
23:41.191 --> 23:44.361
Joseon hasn't existed for over a century.

291
23:45.987 --> 23:47.280
Because of you people.

292
23:47.364 --> 23:48.907
Don't move.

293
23:49.908 --> 23:52.494
-Or you'll break your neck. -Shut up, Chōsenjin.

294
23:57.374 --> 23:58.416
Recognize him?

295
23:59.417 --> 24:00.377
I don't!

296
24:00.460 --> 24:01.878
Who the hell is that?

297
24:04.965 --> 24:06.258
Korean?

298
24:09.886 --> 24:11.012
You…

299
24:11.763 --> 24:13.807
What are you…

300
24:14.891 --> 24:16.184
What are you doing here?

301
24:17.894 --> 24:20.647
He bought drugs from this man in Shinjuku.

302
24:21.648 --> 24:23.650
The Korean victim, Park In-gyu.

303
24:25.777 --> 24:27.362
-That's Takahashi? -Yes.

304
24:29.781 --> 24:32.409
Put it on my tab. I'll pay next time!

305
24:33.994 --> 24:34.828
Move.

306
24:35.412 --> 24:36.663
Hey, Akira! Help me.

307
24:36.746 --> 24:38.248
Isn't that Takahashi?

308
24:39.124 --> 24:41.835
-What's going on here? -Help deal with these bastards.

309
24:41.918 --> 24:43.044
Who the hell are they?

310
24:43.670 --> 24:46.172
How should I know? Some Chōsenjin bastards.

311
24:48.216 --> 24:50.010
We're police.

312
24:51.136 --> 24:52.887
So what?

313
24:53.430 --> 24:55.640
Just because you're cops, you can use violence?

314
24:56.349 --> 24:57.517
You're screwed now.

315
25:02.606 --> 25:05.483
Besides, there's no way a Chōsenjin would be a cop.

316
25:05.984 --> 25:07.527
What a bother.

317
25:09.237 --> 25:10.322
Die!

318
25:38.642 --> 25:40.143
I didn't even strike yet.

319
25:45.482 --> 25:46.650
That's quite enough.

320
25:47.442 --> 25:48.318
Put that down.

321
26:17.764 --> 26:19.849
What do you think you're doing? Let me go!

322
26:20.350 --> 26:24.104
Just get this thing off me!

323
26:24.896 --> 26:26.231
What's this even for?

324
26:27.649 --> 26:29.776
You killed her, didn't you?

325
26:29.859 --> 26:31.403
You killed him, didn't you?

326
26:32.862 --> 26:34.155
What are you talking about?

327
26:36.324 --> 26:37.283
Aki?

328
26:38.326 --> 26:40.161
Hold up. She's dead?

329
26:41.037 --> 26:43.123
You've got to be kidding me.

330
26:43.206 --> 26:44.958
Why would I kill her?

331
26:45.041 --> 26:47.794
We have a witness who saw you with Miyashita Aki

332
26:48.294 --> 26:50.922
a few days before she was killed.

333
26:51.881 --> 26:53.091
That time,

334
26:53.174 --> 26:55.927
she kept whining about wanting to go back home to her parents.

335
26:56.010 --> 26:58.346
So I only roughed her up a bit. I didn't kill her!

336
26:58.430 --> 27:00.640
If you didn't kill her, then who did?

337
27:00.724 --> 27:01.558
What?

338
27:02.100 --> 27:03.143
Well?

339
27:03.226 --> 27:04.269
Anything will do.

340
27:04.769 --> 27:07.355
Just tell us whatever comes to mind.

341
27:09.149 --> 27:11.025
Before I twist your limbs too.

342
27:12.026 --> 27:13.486
Twist my limbs?

343
27:19.701 --> 27:22.537
Are you saying Aki was found dead with twisted limbs?

344
27:22.620 --> 27:23.496
Yes.

345
27:25.457 --> 27:26.708
No way.

346
27:28.710 --> 27:29.753
It was him.

347
27:30.628 --> 27:32.088
The photographer is back.

348
27:32.172 --> 27:33.089
Wait.

349
27:36.092 --> 27:37.343
The photographer?

350
27:39.596 --> 27:40.764
That guy?

351
27:42.724 --> 27:46.227
A few years back, there was a rumor circling among the street gangs.

352
27:46.728 --> 27:50.148
Word was, there was this hitman taking jobs from the yakuza

353
27:50.231 --> 27:53.276
who took pictures of the body after a kill.

354
27:54.486 --> 27:58.698
But it'd be a bit of a stretch to say that he's our culprit.

355
28:00.742 --> 28:06.706
No drugs were used, and there was evidence of sexual assault.

356
28:07.207 --> 28:10.251
Most importantly, the details of the crime itself differ.

357
28:10.335 --> 28:11.920
A different MO from Shinjuku.

358
28:12.003 --> 28:13.171
Why do you ask, sir?

359
28:14.714 --> 28:18.718
And where is this so-called photographer now?

360
28:19.219 --> 28:20.929
He was never arrested.

361
28:21.012 --> 28:23.973
It was a yakuza turf war, so it was hard to intervene.

362
28:24.057 --> 28:25.850
Though the police identified him,

363
28:25.934 --> 28:28.728
they failed to find a single trace of him.

364
28:28.812 --> 28:32.106
It was like the guy didn't even exist.

365
28:32.190 --> 28:35.276
Don't give me that! There might be some connection here!

366
28:35.777 --> 28:37.904
Just look into it.

367
28:45.036 --> 28:47.205
Oh, come on!

368
28:49.624 --> 28:51.042
Hey!

369
28:51.125 --> 28:53.419
Where are you going? Undo this!

370
28:53.503 --> 28:55.088
Take these off before you go!

371
28:55.171 --> 28:58.049
I guess we should look for this prick.

372
28:58.800 --> 29:02.637
The photographer's name is Mikogami… Mikogami Sota?

373
29:03.263 --> 29:05.974
His Korean name is Kim Chang-tae.

374
29:06.057 --> 29:07.475
He's a Zainichi Korean.

375
29:08.226 --> 29:11.229
His whereabouts have been unknown for the past few years.

376
29:13.898 --> 29:16.693
Perhaps he changed his identity and fled overseas?

377
29:18.194 --> 29:21.155
Since he's a Zainichi Korean, he might have gone to Korea.

378
29:22.532 --> 29:26.202
Wherever he is, he can't have stopped killing.

379
29:30.123 --> 29:32.000
Especially the likes of him.

380
29:33.918 --> 29:37.755
You're saying he couldn't stop himself from killing?

381
29:41.259 --> 29:43.428
What if his circumstances forced him to stop?

382
29:44.846 --> 29:46.890
Then he's either dead or already caught.

383
29:47.390 --> 29:49.434
Mikogami…

384
29:50.143 --> 29:51.352
He's in prison?

385
29:52.729 --> 29:53.897
Yeah, maybe.

386
29:55.398 --> 29:56.357
No.

387
29:56.441 --> 29:57.442
Korean.

388
29:58.359 --> 30:02.071
If he's locked up, we would already know his whereabouts.

389
30:03.281 --> 30:06.367
You said Mikogami was a Korean. A Zainichi Korean.

390
30:08.119 --> 30:10.413
What if he kept his Korean nationality?

391
30:10.997 --> 30:13.207
And the Japanese police missed that?

392
30:15.543 --> 30:18.880
So he's not Mikogami Sota

393
30:20.381 --> 30:21.716
but Kim Chang-tae?

394
30:40.151 --> 30:42.028
KANTO FOREIGNERS' PRISON

395
30:42.111 --> 30:43.821
But if he's in here…

396
30:44.322 --> 30:45.990
Let's check it out first.

397
31:11.933 --> 31:14.102
A blind photographer…

398
31:15.019 --> 31:17.397
Not everything is as it seems.

399
31:21.109 --> 31:22.568
A two-shot?

400
31:23.444 --> 31:27.407
So you didn't kill as Mikogami but as Kim Chang-tae.

401
31:28.825 --> 31:31.869
The yakuza are hell-bent on killing you.

402
31:32.954 --> 31:35.498
So you got scared and got locked up?

403
31:36.582 --> 31:38.418
Is it the Shinjuku incident?

404
31:41.421 --> 31:42.547
How did you…

405
31:42.630 --> 31:45.717
The method is similar to my Ikebukuro work.

406
31:46.217 --> 31:48.011
But because I was locked up here,

407
31:48.094 --> 31:51.514
you must have thought someone was copying me.

408
31:51.597 --> 31:53.057
And since they're my copycat,

409
31:53.141 --> 31:56.394
you came here thinking I could give you some sort of lead.

410
31:59.022 --> 32:00.231
Am I wrong?

411
32:01.441 --> 32:04.193
You came here knowing I'm not the culprit, didn't you?

412
32:06.446 --> 32:07.905
A copycat.

413
32:07.989 --> 32:09.490
A Korean?

414
32:10.199 --> 32:11.325
But

415
32:12.535 --> 32:14.871
from what I saw, they're far superior to you.

416
32:15.621 --> 32:16.456
What?

417
32:16.539 --> 32:19.292
I'm saying your copycat seems way more skilled than you.

418
32:20.835 --> 32:24.464
You crudely killed some people and twisted a few of their limbs.

419
32:24.964 --> 32:28.009
But the Shinjuku killer displayed each victim like a work of art.

420
32:29.052 --> 32:30.386
That's how I see it.

421
32:32.013 --> 32:36.142
They're a much more daring, cruel, and creative artist than you.

422
32:37.435 --> 32:39.687
Are you sure you didn't copy Shinjuku?

423
32:42.607 --> 32:45.735
Do you even hear yourself right now?

424
32:47.528 --> 32:49.113
What did you just say?!

425
32:55.953 --> 32:58.164
Hey! Are you okay?

426
32:58.664 --> 33:01.000
Hey!

427
33:05.379 --> 33:07.090
Hey! Calm down.

428
33:07.590 --> 33:09.926
You're not the culprit, or the original.

429
33:11.135 --> 33:13.805
In my opinion, Shinjuku is the original.

430
33:15.556 --> 33:17.058
That punk came first.

431
33:18.559 --> 33:19.477
Isn't that right?

432
33:45.503 --> 33:47.004
How fun.

433
33:47.839 --> 33:48.673
Hey.

434
33:49.173 --> 33:50.883
I'm not following.

435
34:00.935 --> 34:02.812
The original who did it before you.

436
34:06.274 --> 34:07.400
Do you know who it is?

437
34:15.366 --> 34:17.076
Or have you ever met them?

438
34:18.619 --> 34:19.954
The original?

439
34:24.625 --> 34:27.920
I wouldn't know whether Shinjuku is the original or not.

440
34:28.504 --> 34:30.256
But I do know one thing for sure.

441
34:30.965 --> 34:32.341
Before this,

442
34:32.425 --> 34:33.718
a very long time ago,

443
34:34.218 --> 34:37.930
there were bodies with twisted limbs.

444
34:40.224 --> 34:42.351
Have I met them? Don't be ridiculous.

445
34:42.894 --> 34:46.314
I just picked it up from old newspapers.

446
34:48.608 --> 34:49.567
Why?

447
34:50.109 --> 34:51.277
Are you disappointed?

448
34:57.283 --> 35:00.036
I may not know who that killer is,

449
35:00.786 --> 35:05.249
but it's been so long that I figured they were either caught or dead.

450
35:06.959 --> 35:08.294
Or back from the dead?

451
35:11.464 --> 35:13.549
So? Are you two going to try and catch them?

452
35:15.968 --> 35:18.221
Hey, guard!

453
35:19.096 --> 35:21.390
To the infirmary!

454
35:28.022 --> 35:30.441
I wish you two detectives the best of luck.

455
35:34.237 --> 35:36.280
Hey!

456
35:40.201 --> 35:43.162
You're just a murderer, and you think you can play the expert?

457
35:45.164 --> 35:49.252
You're just a criminal who'll rot in here for the rest of his life.

458
35:49.335 --> 35:50.419
Don't forget that.

459
35:52.171 --> 35:56.259
That bastard seems to know a thing or two, but I guess you don't.

460
36:22.868 --> 36:24.620
Where are we going at this hour?

461
36:27.039 --> 36:29.834
I want to go home, too, you know.

462
36:51.814 --> 36:55.484
My deepest condolences for your loss.

463
36:56.736 --> 36:58.821
We failed to protect your daughter.

464
36:59.530 --> 37:02.491
As a police officer, I sincerely apologize.

465
37:03.451 --> 37:04.952
I am so sorry.

466
37:13.210 --> 37:15.671
We will catch the criminal, no matter what.

467
37:23.721 --> 37:25.306
I sincerely apologize.

468
37:29.310 --> 37:32.355
It seems I failed to raise my daughter right.

469
37:36.734 --> 37:39.070
She was always a problem child.

470
37:40.613 --> 37:43.157
She had no ounce of gratitude toward her parents.

471
37:45.993 --> 37:47.995
Running away from home, doing drugs…

472
37:50.831 --> 37:53.501
She was a disgrace to the family.

473
37:55.711 --> 37:57.254
A part of me always felt…

474
37:59.298 --> 38:01.801
that she may end up dying like this.

475
38:03.928 --> 38:06.555
Sorry for the trouble of making you come all this way.

476
38:07.264 --> 38:08.516
I'm so sorry.

477
38:08.599 --> 38:10.101
I'm truly sorry.

478
38:12.144 --> 38:13.771
We're truly sorry.

479
38:14.271 --> 38:16.982
We are truly sorry.

480
38:17.066 --> 38:18.609
We are so sorry.

481
38:30.162 --> 38:31.372
You…

482
38:34.542 --> 38:36.043
don't have to apologize so much…

483
38:36.627 --> 38:37.837
You two!

484
38:37.920 --> 38:39.505
Why are you apologizing?!

485
38:41.215 --> 38:42.842
Your daughter is dead.

486
38:42.925 --> 38:45.094
Why are you talking like it's not your problem?

487
38:47.012 --> 38:48.472
Your daughter…

488
38:49.181 --> 38:51.809
She didn't do anything bad enough to deserve death!

489
38:53.686 --> 38:54.895
Until the very end,

490
38:56.313 --> 38:58.232
she said she missed her mom and dad.

491
38:58.732 --> 39:01.193
That she wanted to go home!

492
39:03.487 --> 39:05.114
So, please.

493
39:06.699 --> 39:09.201
Don't apologize at a time like this.

494
39:19.545 --> 39:20.921
Let's go.

495
39:52.203 --> 39:53.537
Hey, Korean.

496
39:56.582 --> 40:00.753
In a world this shitty, what's the point in catching criminals?

497
40:05.466 --> 40:06.467
Hey.

498
40:08.802 --> 40:10.387
It's not a big deal, but…

499
40:13.974 --> 40:16.101
From now on, don't call me "Korean."

500
40:18.103 --> 40:19.480
Please call me by my name.

501
40:20.356 --> 40:21.440
Like Kim Seok,

502
40:22.066 --> 40:23.400
or Detective Kim.

503
40:27.154 --> 40:28.489
I understand.

504
40:30.449 --> 40:31.534
I'm sorry,

505
40:32.326 --> 40:33.452
Detective Kim.

506
40:37.164 --> 40:38.123
So?

507
40:41.377 --> 40:42.795
You're not gonna catch them?

508
40:52.304 --> 40:54.890
I really can't help myself today.

509
41:03.816 --> 41:05.109
Can I also get a light?

510
41:18.581 --> 41:20.708
-So… -It just doesn't make any sense.

511
41:23.168 --> 41:25.671
You came to investigate a murder that happened in Korea

512
41:27.006 --> 41:31.218
and just happened to come across an identical crime scene?

513
41:34.096 --> 41:35.180
That's impossible.

514
41:37.433 --> 41:39.435
It's not like you have superpowers.

515
41:39.518 --> 41:41.687
And what's all this about the "original"?

516
41:47.276 --> 41:48.485
The original.

517
41:57.036 --> 41:59.997
The old newspaper Kim Chang-tae mentioned earlier.

518
42:04.668 --> 42:06.045
A very long time ago…

519
42:08.339 --> 42:10.883
back in Korea in the '80s…

520
42:15.846 --> 42:19.058
a body was found with twisted limbs.

521
42:21.935 --> 42:22.853
What?

522
42:26.065 --> 42:28.651
And then, there were more.

523
42:29.443 --> 42:30.569
For a long time now,

524
42:32.446 --> 42:33.530
this case…

525
42:35.658 --> 42:37.743
has been repeating itself.

526
42:42.164 --> 42:43.040
The killer

527
42:43.874 --> 42:45.459
has returned.

528
46:42.905 --> 46:46.450
THIS SERIES IS A WORK OF FICTION, INSPIRED BY HISTORICAL EVENTS

529
46:50.996 --> 46:54.499
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
